Z||000000||sully5||04-24-2000||11:49 AM||||How do I get in to remove my speedometer? I tried yesterday using both the Haynes and Chilton manuals, but couldn't make much sense of those. Did a search on past posts but could not locate anything. Appreciate any help. sully||||reg||5
Z||000001||coyote||04-24-2000||02:20 PM||||1. remove the 4 7mm screws from the steering columncover.<P>2. remove the 4 screws on the gauge bezel and remove.<P>3. remove the 7 screws from the rear gauge pod cover 3 on top 2 in the back and 2 underneath, remove cover.<P>4. remove all the switches; headlight,defroster etc, and disconnect the wiring harness's<P>5. remove the 3 connecters to the gauge pack, left rear, right rear, bottom left.<P>6. there will also be som clips on the switch harness that will nedd to be removed.<P>7. remove 6 screw from po bracket 2 10mm in the back, 2 7mm in front and 2 10mm underneath.<P>8. pull out pod and remove cluster (3 7mm at the top in back).<P>9. Remove the 5.5 mm screws that hold the lens and metal backing on.<BR>you now have acces to the speedo.<P>I am writing this from memory so i may have missed a screw here or there, the guys here will fill in the blanks.<P>Coyote||||reg||1
Z||000002||sully5||04-24-2000||08:03 PM||||Thanks for the input coyote.||||reg||1
